<title>ITALY: Italian Oct car registrations rose 22.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Italian Oct car registrations rose 22.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian new car registrations rose 22.88 percent to 144,500 units in October, compared with 117,598 units in October 1995, the Ministry of Transport said in a statement.</p>
<p>This compared with an 8.55 percent fall in September to 116,000 units.</p>
<p>In the first 10 months of this year new car registrations rose 0.57 percent to 1,488,979 units.  </p>
<p>	   Oct 96 registrations Mkt shre   Oct 95   Mkt shre</p>
<p>Fiat	     62,150   43.01	 52,723  48.83</p>
<p>Volkswagen     16,850   11.66	 14,069  11.96</p>
<p>Ford	     11,950    8.27	  9,686   8.24</p>
<p>PSA Peugeot    10,750    7.47	  9,714   8.26</p>
<p>Renault	   8,650    5.99	  7,830   6.66</p>
<p>BMW		 7,300    5.05	  4,649   3.95</p>
<p>Mercedes	  3,480    2.41	  2,185   1.86</p>
<p>Nissan	    3,150    2.18	  2,668   2.27</p>
<p>Volvo	     2,600    1.80	  1,747   1.49</p>
<p>NOTE - Fiat comprises Fiat, Alfa Romeo, Lancia Autobianchi, and Fiat-Innocenti. Volkswagen comprises VW, Audi, Skoda and Seat. General Motors comprises Opel and Saab. PSA-Peugeot comprises Peugeot and Citroen. BMW comprises BMW and Rover.</p>
<p>-- Rome bureau +396 6782505</p>
</text>
